!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Liver metastasis
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: Liver metastasis
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = age: 57
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = Sex: M
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: gemcitabine, ADH1, cisplatin
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Samples were flash frozen in liquid nitrogen, cryo-sectioned and H&E stained. After sectioning onto the Visium slides, sample processing was performed as described in the Visium 10x Genomics protocol for fresh-frozen tissue samples (15 minutes were used for permealization time).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Library preparation was performed as described in  the Visium Spatial Gene Expression Reagent Kit (PN-1000189), Library Construction Kit (PN-1000196), and Dual Index Plate TT Set A (PN-3000431) as described in the Visium protocol for fresh frozen tissue samples (CG000239).
!Sample_description = Fresh frozen Visium ST sequencing
!Sample_data_processing = The demultiplexed reads were processed using Space Ranger (v.1.3.1) from 10x Genomics, aligned to the GRCh38 reference genome with default parameters. The resulting unique molecular identifier (UMI) count matrices were then analysed using Seurat (v.4.3) 47 in the R platform (v.4.2.0). Detailed quality control (QC) metrics were generated and evaluated, and spots were carefully filtered to obtain high-quality SRT data for downstream analyses. Briefly, for basic quality filtering, spots with low complexity libraries (UMI count below 100) were filtered out to eliminate low-quality spots. Additionally, spots located within acellular stromal interfaces were excluded and samples with more than 40% low-quality spots were also excluded from subsequent analyses.
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: GRCh38 reference genome
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: spatial.tar.gz : Compressed tar archives include processed output from Space Ranger with spatial information
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: filtered_feature_bc_matrix.h5 : Filtered feature-barcode matrices in HDF5 format
!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: Spatial Transcriptomics
!Sample_platform_id = GPL24676
